    "turn_text": "Well, I heard I didn't hear her say today, but I've heard her say today just because you have record turnout doesn't mean you don't have suppression. And I'm just not sure how those can be mutually exclusive. If you have record turnout, how are you? So there's a argument that it would be more than a record turnout. It just, it seems like that what they were saying was in 2020, Joe Biden won Georgia. So the Republicans are putting in place where you couldn't have that number of votes and that couldn't happen again. You know, it's just false. I mean, she can say what she wants to say. It's just not accurate. I think the facts, it's hard to argue with facts. You can say your emotion, but when the facts are on the ground, how do you have Suppression and record turn and and and I'm open if they can point to people who should have been allowed to vote that were denied voting then I think we should absolutely address it but it's this blanket statement of their suppression and tell me people who showed up to vote they were legal to vote they were eligible to vote and they didn't get the opportunity to vote and that absolutely should be addressed because I think Michael Adams our Secretary of State says it should be easy to vote and hard to cheat and uh... there's a balance you just can't have no checks and checks at all because it makes it easier to cheat and so uh... when people say there's voter suppression gimme evidence of it that's what i asked for",
