    "turn_text": "so what so almost all health care goes to the energy and commerce committee there's a way the means committee they do some health care more some funding of health care but everything almost everything dealing with medicare everything everything dealing with medicaid health insurance, health insurance policy, so the Affordable Care Act, Obamacare, all that came through the Energy and Commerce Committee. So we're going to focus on some things knowing that, and I should be able to chair that subcommittee, which is on the Energy and Commerce School Committee. And we know that currently there's 51 U.S. senators, but even when we were kind of forming our agendas, we thought we were going to take the majority. We knew that Joe Biden was still going to be president. So we knew that we're not going to be able to repeal and replace the Affordable Care Act although it's an unsustainable situation. But there are things we can do. We want people to know what the prices are of what they, just the stuff that people do with everyday price transparency. Why does something cost when you go to the doctor? When you go to the hospital, you get a bill. And three months later for numbers that you say, I had no idea that's what was going on moving forward. And so we're really going to look at just the operation of the healthcare system. How do you get pre-authorized if you're going to have a surgery, then all of a sudden you get trapped in insurance? going back and forth. So those kind of things that, you know, aren't big headlines, but they're important. But the other thing is we'll have oversight of the Wuhan lab. And I think it's in a Center for Disease Control. And we're going to investigate to get answers so we can get solutions because, you know, I think the American people need to know did the Wuhan lab leak, did it come from the Wuhan lab, but also importantly, why did the NIH under the direction of Dr. Fauci and his group It immediately dismissed that. We know that it probably came from the lab. We do know there's no evidence to say it didn't come from the lab. There was never any evidence to say that. And within a week or two of all this breaking, the NIH, under Dr. Fauci, essentially put out its conspiracy to say that. You know, Twitter took down that you could even tweet that it.",
